            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Federal Loan Consolidation: This combines multiple federal loans into a single Direct Consolidation Loan with one monthly payment and one loan servicer. The new interest rate is the weighted average of your existing loan rates, rounded up to the nearest one-eighth percent. Consolidation does not lower your interest rate. Its primary benefit is administrative simplification and potential access to repayment plans that your original loans may not have been eligible for. Importantly, consolidation resets the qualifying payment counter for PSLF and IDR forgiveness. If you have been making payments toward forgiveness, consolidating can erase that progress."
